WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.531 --> 00:00:18.198
On the 17th of October, 2009,

00:00:18.222 --> 00:00:22.690
President Mohamed Nasheed of the Maldives
did something unusual.

00:00:23.811 --> 00:00:27.374
He held his cabinet meeting underwater.

00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:36.130
He literally took his ministers
scuba diving, as it were,

00:00:36.154 --> 00:00:40.633
to warn the world
that his country could drown

00:00:40.657 --> 00:00:42.979
unless we control global warming.

00:00:43.741 --> 00:00:47.146
Now I don't know whether he got
his message across to the world or not,

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.929
but he certainly caught mine.

00:00:49.908 --> 00:00:51.868
I saw a political stunt.

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:54.577
You see, I'm a politician,

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:56.520
and I notice these things.

00:00:57.108 --> 00:00:58.751
And let's be honest,

00:00:58.775 --> 00:01:02.750
the Maldives are distant
from where I come from --

00:01:02.774 --> 00:01:04.493
my country is Bhutan --

00:01:04.517 --> 00:01:08.258
so I didn't lose any sleep
over their impending fate.

00:01:09.375 --> 00:01:13.638
Barely two months later,
I saw another political stunt.

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:18.098
This time, the prime minister of Nepal,

00:01:18.122 --> 00:01:21.845
he held his cabinet meeting
on Mount Everest.

00:01:23.102 --> 00:01:28.428
He took all his ministers all the way up
to the base camp of Everest

00:01:28.452 --> 00:01:30.394
to warn the world

00:01:30.418 --> 00:01:32.379
that the Himalayan glaciers were melting.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.869
Now did that worry me?

00:01:34.893 --> 00:01:36.139
You bet it did.

00:01:36.163 --> 00:01:37.527
I live in the Himalayas.

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:42.130
But did I lose any sleep over his message?

00:01:43.205 --> 00:01:44.355
No.

00:01:44.748 --> 00:01:50.579
I wasn't ready to let a political stunt
interfere with my beauty sleep.

00:01:50.952 --> 00:01:52.722
(Laughter)

00:01:52.746 --> 00:01:54.428
Now fast-forward 10 years.

00:01:55.865 --> 00:01:58.386
In February this year,

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.690
I saw this report.

00:02:02.163 --> 00:02:06.154
This here report basically concludes

00:02:06.178 --> 00:02:12.332
that one-third of the ice
on the Hindu Kush Himalaya mountains

00:02:12.356 --> 00:02:14.469
could melt by the end of the century.

00:02:15.085 --> 00:02:17.380
But that's only if,

00:02:17.404 --> 00:02:20.611
if we are able to contain global warming

00:02:20.635 --> 00:02:24.916
to 1.5 degrees centigrade
over preindustrial levels.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:27.810
Otherwise, if we can't,

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:29.817
the glaciers would melt much faster.

00:02:32.766 --> 00:02:36.149
1.5 degrees Celsius. "No way," I thought.

00:02:36.173 --> 00:02:39.490
Even the Paris Agreement's
ambitious targets

00:02:39.514 --> 00:02:42.750
aimed to limit global warming
to two degrees centigrade.

00:02:43.317 --> 00:02:47.822
1.5 degrees centigrade is what they call
the best-case scenario.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.484
"Now this can't be true," I thought.

00:02:51.508 --> 00:02:53.662
The Hindu Kush Himalaya region

00:02:53.686 --> 00:02:57.512
is the world's third-largest
repository of ice,

00:02:57.536 --> 00:02:59.186
after the North and South Poles.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:01.781
That's why we are also called
the "Third Pole."

00:03:02.361 --> 00:03:04.527
There's a lot of ice in the region.

00:03:05.377 --> 00:03:07.860
And yes, the glaciers, they are melting.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.535
We know that.

00:03:10.253 --> 00:03:12.092
I have been to those in my country.

00:03:12.116 --> 00:03:14.217
I've seen them, and yes, they are melting.

00:03:14.241 --> 00:03:15.798
They are vulnerable.

00:03:15.822 --> 00:03:18.734
"But they can't be that vulnerable,"
I remember thinking.

00:03:21.275 --> 00:03:22.774
But what if they are?

00:03:23.739 --> 00:03:27.675
What if our glaciers melt
much more quickly than I anticipate?

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:32.944
What if our glaciers are much more
vulnerable than previously thought?

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:36.439
And what if, as a result,
the glacial lakes --

00:03:36.463 --> 00:03:39.368
now these are lakes
that form when glaciers melt --

00:03:39.392 --> 00:03:43.233
what if those lakes burst
under the weight of additional water?

00:03:44.585 --> 00:03:47.354
And what if those floods
cascade into other glacial lakes,

00:03:47.378 --> 00:03:49.481
creating even bigger outbursts?

00:03:50.452 --> 00:03:54.227
That would create unprecedented
flash floods in my country.

00:03:55.113 --> 00:03:57.271
That would wreck my country.

00:03:58.302 --> 00:04:00.914
That would wreak havoc in my country.

00:04:00.938 --> 00:04:04.478
That would have the potential
to literally destroy our land,

00:04:04.502 --> 00:04:07.009
our livelihood, our way of life.

00:04:10.491 --> 00:04:14.371
So that report caught my attention

00:04:14.395 --> 00:04:17.735
in ways that political stunts couldn't.

00:04:17.759 --> 00:04:18.948
It was put together

00:04:18.972 --> 00:04:23.537
by the International Centre for Integrated
Mountain Development, or ICIMOD,

00:04:23.561 --> 00:04:24.846
which is based in Nepal.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:30.315
Scientists and experts have studied
our glaciers for decades,

00:04:30.339 --> 00:04:35.060
and their report kept me awake at night,
agonizing about the bad news

00:04:35.084 --> 00:04:37.395
and what it meant for my country

00:04:37.419 --> 00:04:38.569
and my people.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.973
So after several sleepless nights,

00:04:41.997 --> 00:04:45.170
I went to Nepal to visit ICIMOD.

00:04:46.892 --> 00:04:51.296
I found a team of highly competent
and dedicated scientists there,

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:52.939
and here's what they told me.

00:04:53.828 --> 00:04:54.978
Number one:

00:04:55.706 --> 00:04:59.976
the Hindu Kush Himalaya glaciers
have been melting for some time now.

00:05:01.716 --> 00:05:04.730
Take that glacier, for instance.

00:05:05.278 --> 00:05:07.096
It's on Mount Everest.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:12.604
As you can see, this once massive glacier
has already lost much of its ice.

00:05:14.029 --> 00:05:15.538
Number two:

00:05:15.562 --> 00:05:17.912
the glaciers are now melting
much more quickly --

00:05:17.936 --> 00:05:24.185
so quickly, in fact, that at just
1.5 degrees centigrade of global warming,

00:05:24.209 --> 00:05:26.891
one-third of the glaciers would melt.

00:05:28.084 --> 00:05:31.305
At two degrees centigrade
of global warming,

00:05:31.329 --> 00:05:33.791
half the glaciers would disappear.

00:05:33.815 --> 00:05:36.941
And if current trends were to continue,

00:05:36.965 --> 00:05:40.434
a full two-thirds
of our glaciers would vanish.

00:05:42.339 --> 00:05:43.489
Number three:

00:05:44.295 --> 00:05:49.469
global warming means that our mountains
receive more rain and less snow ...

00:05:50.779 --> 00:05:54.481
and, unlike snowfall, rain melts ice,

00:05:54.505 --> 00:05:57.282
which just hurts
the health of our glaciers.

00:05:58.397 --> 00:05:59.547
Number four:

00:06:01.457 --> 00:06:04.458
pollution in the region has increased
the amount of black carbon

00:06:04.482 --> 00:06:06.642
that's deposited on our glaciers.

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:08.021
Black carbon is like soot.

00:06:08.045 --> 00:06:10.346
Black carbon absorbs heat

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.774
and just accelerates
the melting of glaciers.

00:06:14.243 --> 00:06:15.393
To summarize,

00:06:16.344 --> 00:06:18.592
our glaciers are melting rapidly,

00:06:19.775 --> 00:06:23.251
and global warming is making them
melt much more quickly.

00:06:25.036 --> 00:06:26.362
But what does this mean?

00:06:27.539 --> 00:06:32.310
It means that the 240 million people

00:06:32.334 --> 00:06:34.843
who live in the Hindu Kush
Himalaya region --

00:06:34.867 --> 00:06:40.119
in Afghanistan, Pakistan, India,
China, Nepal, Bangladesh, Myanmar

00:06:40.143 --> 00:06:42.769
and my own beloved country, Bhutan --

00:06:42.793 --> 00:06:44.959
these people will be directly affected.

00:06:46.932 --> 00:06:48.875
When glaciers melt,

00:06:48.899 --> 00:06:50.816
when there's more rain and less snow,

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:55.117
there will be huge changes
in the way water behaves.

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:57.437
There will be more extremes:

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:01.966
more intense rain,
more flash floods, more landslides,

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:04.928
more glacial lake outburst floods.

00:07:04.952 --> 00:07:09.364
All this will cause
unimaginable destruction

00:07:09.388 --> 00:07:13.959
in a region that already has
some of the poorest people on earth.

00:07:15.971 --> 00:07:18.797
But it's not just the people
in the immediate region

00:07:18.821 --> 00:07:20.110
who'll be affected.

00:07:20.134 --> 00:07:23.605
People living downstream
will also be hit hard.

00:07:25.619 --> 00:07:30.318
That's because 10 of their major rivers

00:07:30.342 --> 00:07:33.186
originate in the Hindu Kush
Himalaya mountains.

00:07:34.031 --> 00:07:38.564
These rivers provide
critical water for agriculture

00:07:38.588 --> 00:07:40.042
and drinking water

00:07:40.066 --> 00:07:45.070
to more than 1.6 billion people
living downstream.

00:07:45.094 --> 00:07:47.578
That's one in five humans.

00:07:49.149 --> 00:07:51.254
That's why the Hindu Kush
Himalaya mountains

00:07:51.278 --> 00:07:53.713
are also called
the "water towers of Asia."

00:07:55.815 --> 00:07:57.219
But when glaciers melt,

00:07:58.213 --> 00:07:59.830
when monsoons turn severe,

00:07:59.854 --> 00:08:02.608
those rivers will obviously flood,

00:08:03.432 --> 00:08:06.401
so there will be deluges
when water is not required

00:08:06.425 --> 00:08:09.156
and droughts will be very common,

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:11.123
when water is desperately required.

00:08:11.147 --> 00:08:16.942
In short, Asia's water tower
will be broken,

00:08:16.966 --> 00:08:23.037
and that will be disastrous
for one-fifth of humanity.

00:08:26.765 --> 00:08:28.407
Should the rest of the world care?

00:08:29.899 --> 00:08:32.050
Should you, for instance, care?

00:08:32.472 --> 00:08:35.645
Remember, I didn't care
when I heard that the Maldives

00:08:35.669 --> 00:08:37.520
could disappear underwater.

00:08:37.544 --> 00:08:40.670
And that is the crux
of the problem, isn't it?

00:08:40.694 --> 00:08:42.273
We don't care.

00:08:44.428 --> 00:08:47.043
We don't care until
we are personally affected.

00:08:47.729 --> 00:08:50.420
I mean, we know.
We know climate change is real.

00:08:50.444 --> 00:08:53.012
We know that we face
drastic and dramatic change.

00:08:53.036 --> 00:08:54.526
We know that it is coming fast.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:56.359
Yet most of us

00:08:57.662 --> 00:09:00.947
act as if everything were normal.

00:09:02.359 --> 00:09:03.724
So we must care,

00:09:04.726 --> 00:09:06.308
all of us,

00:09:06.332 --> 00:09:11.046
and if you can't care for those who are
affected by the melting of glaciers,

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:13.033
you should at least care for yourself.

00:09:14.193 --> 00:09:17.266
That's because the Hindu Kush
Himalaya mountains --

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:20.741
the entire region
is like the pulse of the planet.

00:09:22.819 --> 00:09:25.191
If the region falls sick,

00:09:25.215 --> 00:09:27.960
the entire planet will eventually suffer.

00:09:29.164 --> 00:09:30.314
And right now,

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:33.646
with our glaciers melting rapidly,

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.511
the region is not just sick --

00:09:35.535 --> 00:09:37.361
it is crying out for help.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:42.254
And how will it affect
the rest of the world?

00:09:42.278 --> 00:09:46.664
One obvious scenario
is the potential destabilization

00:09:46.688 --> 00:09:50.562
caused by tens of millions
of climate refugees,

00:09:50.586 --> 00:09:53.763
who'll be forced to move
because they have no or little water,

00:09:53.787 --> 00:09:56.748
or because their livelihoods
have been destroyed

00:09:56.772 --> 00:09:58.475
by the melting of glaciers.

00:09:59.391 --> 00:10:03.116
Another scenario we can't take lightly

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:06.066
is the potential of conflict over water

00:10:07.409 --> 00:10:14.329
and the political destabilization
in a region that has three nuclear powers:

00:10:14.353 --> 00:10:18.575
China, India, Pakistan.

00:10:21.175 --> 00:10:26.439
I believe that the situation
in our region is grave enough

00:10:26.463 --> 00:10:31.080
to warrant the creation
of a new intergovernmental agency.

00:10:32.022 --> 00:10:35.877
So as a native
from that part of the world,

00:10:35.901 --> 00:10:39.116
I want to propose here, today,

00:10:39.140 --> 00:10:42.203
the establishment
of the Third Pole Council,

00:10:43.846 --> 00:10:47.342
a high-level,
intergovernmental organization

00:10:47.366 --> 00:10:51.030
tasked with the singular responsibility

00:10:51.054 --> 00:10:54.449
of protecting the world's
third-largest repository of ice.

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:57.848
A Third Pole Council

00:10:57.872 --> 00:11:01.819
would consist of all eight countries
located in the region

00:11:01.843 --> 00:11:03.101
as member countries,

00:11:03.125 --> 00:11:05.763
as equal member countries,

00:11:05.787 --> 00:11:08.533
and could also include
representative organizations

00:11:08.557 --> 00:11:12.311
and other countries
who have vested interests in the region

00:11:12.335 --> 00:11:13.891
as non-voting members.

00:11:13.915 --> 00:11:15.969
But the big idea

00:11:15.993 --> 00:11:19.556
is to get all stakeholders together
to work together.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:24.124
To work together to monitor
the health of the glaciers;

00:11:24.148 --> 00:11:29.028
to work together to shape and implement
policies to protect our glaciers,

00:11:29.052 --> 00:11:30.803
and, by extension,

00:11:30.827 --> 00:11:35.951
to protect the billions of people
who depend on our glaciers.

00:11:37.602 --> 00:11:39.009
We have to work together,

00:11:40.783 --> 00:11:45.354
because thinking globally,
acting locally ...

00:11:46.552 --> 00:11:47.991
does not work.

00:11:48.015 --> 00:11:49.490
We've tried that in Bhutan.

00:11:50.463 --> 00:11:54.720
We've made immense sacrifices
to act locally ...

00:11:56.705 --> 00:12:01.831
and while individual localized efforts
will continue to be important,

00:12:01.855 --> 00:12:05.308
they cannot stand up
to the onslaught of climate change.

00:12:05.677 --> 00:12:09.407
To stand up to climate change,
we must work together.

00:12:10.272 --> 00:12:13.931
We must think globally and act regionally.

00:12:15.017 --> 00:12:18.932
Our entire region must come together,

00:12:18.956 --> 00:12:20.498
to work together,

00:12:20.522 --> 00:12:22.484
to fight climate change together,

00:12:22.508 --> 00:12:25.252
to make our voices heard together.

00:12:27.751 --> 00:12:32.068
And that includes India and China.

00:12:32.836 --> 00:12:34.901
They must step up their game.

00:12:36.197 --> 00:12:40.879
They must take the ownership
of the fight to protect our glaciers.

00:12:41.482 --> 00:12:44.544
And for that, these two countries,
these two powerful giants,

00:12:44.568 --> 00:12:47.419
must reduce their own greenhouse gases,

00:12:48.646 --> 00:12:51.475
control their pollution,
and lead the fight.

00:12:53.134 --> 00:12:56.428
Lead the global fight
against climate change.

00:12:57.950 --> 00:13:00.886
And all that with a renewed
sense of urgency.

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:04.908
Only then -- and that, too, only maybe --

00:13:04.932 --> 00:13:06.808
will our region

00:13:06.832 --> 00:13:09.268
and other regions
that depend on our glaciers

00:13:09.292 --> 00:13:13.855
have any chance to avoid
major catastrophes.

00:13:15.554 --> 00:13:16.998
Time is running out.

00:13:18.257 --> 00:13:21.526
We must act together, now.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:28.899
Otherwise, the next time
Nepal's cabinet meets on Mount Everest,

00:13:28.923 --> 00:13:31.226
that spectacular backdrop ...

00:13:32.534 --> 00:13:34.018
may look quite different.

00:13:37.316 --> 00:13:38.466
And if that happens,

00:13:40.031 --> 00:13:42.244
if our glaciers melt,

00:13:42.268 --> 00:13:45.673
rising sea levels
could well drown the Maldives.

00:13:47.229 --> 00:13:51.551
And while they can hold
their cabinet meetings underwater

00:13:51.575 --> 00:13:54.226
to send an SOS to the world,

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:56.679
their country can keep existing

00:13:56.703 --> 00:14:01.083
only if their islands keep existing.

00:14:03.256 --> 00:14:07.931
The Maldives are still distant, away.

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:12.669
Their islands are distant
from where I live.

00:14:13.927 --> 00:14:19.498
But now, I pay close attention
to what happens out there.

00:14:21.259 --> 00:14:24.023
Thank you very much.

00:14:24.047 --> 00:14:28.507
(Applause)

